<%# locals: (node:, library_path:, return_to:) %>
<%# RENAME OR MOVE (F; user stories 1.3 and 4.7), shared by the Library's inspector and the file
    page the way files/_meta and files/_attach are, and placed under _meta on both, beside the name
    and the location it changes. Both forms post to Maker::MoveNode behind FilesController#rename
    and #move. Both callers render it for a FILE outside a git working tree and for nothing else,
    which is exactly what the controller accepts: folders wait for Share#move to rewrite a subtree's
    paths (FilesController::FOLDERS_NOT_YET), and bytes git owns never go through the port
    (docs/invariants/git-editing.md).

    CLOSED UNTIL ASKED FOR, as the note and link composers on the file page are. A details.menu was
    the other candidate and is the wrong one: menu_controller.js closes a menu on any click outside
    it, and the folder chooser's modal is appended to the body, so the menu would shut under the
    maker halfway through choosing.

    FLAT FIELD NAMES (CLAUDE.md 14d). A form_with with neither model nor scope has a blank
    object_name, and the controller reads params[:name] and params[:parent_node_id]; the _tag
    helpers cannot nest them, and files_rename_move_test.rb asserts the rendered names.
    `return_to` is the attach control's allowlisted flag, "library" from the inspector.

    THE CHOOSER STARTS ON THE FOLDER THE NODE IS IN NOW, labelled in the chooser's own spelling
    ("/a/b", or its root label). `library_path` is FilesController#library_path_for, the folder
    then the name, and a name is one segment, so its dirname is the folder. NIL MEANS A BROKEN
    ANCESTOR CHAIN, and the label says "Current folder" rather than claim the root: a label that
    disagrees with the value is wrong in the direction that looks like it worked
    (lib/file_chooser.js). The chooser writes "" for the root, which the controller reads as the
    root. %>
<%
  folder = library_path && File.dirname(library_path)
  folder_label = if folder.nil? then "Current folder"
                 elsif folder == "." then "/ (library root)"
                 else "/#{folder}"
                 end
%>
<details class="rename-move composer">
  <summary class="btn small">Rename or move…</summary>
  <%= form_with url: rename_file_path(node.node_id), method: :patch, class: "menu-form",
                data: { turbo: false } do %>
    <%= hidden_field_tag :return_to, return_to, id: nil %>
    <label class="menu-form-label" for="rename_<%= node.node_id %>">New name</label>
    <span class="menu-form-row">
      <%= text_field_tag :name, node.name, id: "rename_#{node.node_id}", required: true,
                         autocomplete: "off", spellcheck: false %>
      <%= submit_tag "Rename", class: "small", name: nil %>
    </span>
  <% end %>
  <%= form_with url: move_file_path(node.node_id), method: :patch, class: "menu-form",
                data: { turbo: false } do %>
    <%= hidden_field_tag :return_to, return_to, id: nil %>
    <span class="menu-form-label">Move to folder</span>
    <%# panel-actions WRAPS where menu-form-row does not: the chooser's button keeps its path's
        width (up to 260px), and in the 300px inspector a long path would otherwise push Move out
        of the panel. %>
    <span class="panel-actions">
      <%= render "shared/folder_field", name: "parent_node_id",
                 children_url: library_children_path, create_url: library_folders_path,
                 value: node.parent_node_id.to_s, label: folder_label %>
      <%= submit_tag "Move", class: "small", name: nil %>
    </span>
  <% end %>
</details>
